#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build the Call_Inventory of an Upstream tree at one pin (Spike S2).

usage: tools/inventory [--out-dir DIR] <upstream-dir> <pin>

Scans every file under bin/, install/, migrations/, default/, config/ and
shell/ of <upstream-dir> that is a shell script (sh, bash, dash, zsh or ksh
shebang; .sh, .bash, .zsh or .ksh name; or a shell file Upstream sources
without a shebang: bashrc, files under a bash/ or uwsm/ folder) or a file
that runs commands:

  *.lua                Hyprland Lua config. String literals on lines with
                       exec_cmd, launch, bind and similar calls are commands;
                       other string literals are analysed as uncertain.
  *.conf (Hyprland)    exec, exec-once, execr, execr-once, exec-shutdown and
                       bind* lines with the exec dispatcher.
  *.desktop            Exec= and TryExec= lines.
  systemd units        Exec*= lines (*.service, *.timer, *.socket, *.path,
                       *.target and drop-in *.conf files).
  *.json, *.jsonc      action, when, checked, disabled, exec, command, cmd,
                       run and on-click* values.
  *.toml, *.yaml, *.yml, *.ini
                       command, cmd, exec, run, shell and on-click* values
                       (uncertain).
  *.qml, *.js, *.mjs, scripts with another interpreter
                       string literals; a line with a string array is read
                       as one argv.

Writes into DIR (default: compat/inventory/ in this repository):

  <pin>.tsv          <file> TAB <line> TAB <class> TAB <detail>, one line per
                     finding, sorted by file, line number, class and detail
  <pin>.summary.md   counts per class and the lists reviews need

Classes:
  arch-tool     call of an Arch tool (ARCH_TOOLS, limine-*); detail: the
                command and its first three arguments
  arch-path     reference to an Arch path (ARCH_PATHS); detail: the path
  privileged    sudo, pkexec, doas, run0 (Upstream's as_root helper is
                marked uncertain); detail: the command run with privilege
  home-write    write into the home folder; detail: the target, with ~ for
                $HOME and the XDG base folders, and " [namespaced]" under
                ~/.config/omarchy, ~/.local/share/omarchy,
                ~/.local/state/omarchy or ~/.cache/omarchy
  user-unit     systemctl --user unit verbs (detail "<unit> (<verb>)"),
                environment imports into the user manager (detail
                "environment (<command>)"), writes under ~/.config/systemd
                (detail: the path)
  session       uwsm, uwsm-app, Hyprland, start-hyprland, hyprctl dispatch
                exec; detail: the command
  omarchy-path  reference to $OMARCHY_PATH, ~/.local/share/omarchy or
                /usr/share/omarchy; detail: the referenced path with its base

A detail ending in " ?" is uncertain: a target resolved through a variable,
a command found in a string that is probably run, or a tool name passed as
an argument. Comments and here-doc bodies are not analysed. The line is the
line where the command starts.

Exit codes: 0 written, 1 output could not be written, 2 usage or input error.
"""

